Z||000002||FieroJoe||02-23-2001||09:13 PM||||The way I hear it, was the Chevy wouldnt let Pontiac put make the Fieros any faster and with better tuned engines because they would compete so well with the corvette, probably causing the corvette's sales to drop so much that they would have to phase it (the corvette) out.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||02-23-2001||09:25 PM||||There were a lot of rumors flying in the mid 80's about the future of performance cars. There was even talk of completly phasing out the v8 engine altogther. Experiments were done with smaller engines that would keep a high level of performance, such as GM's twin engine Citation with 2 aluminum block 3.1's. If the 'Vette were to have been phased out, then another smaller displacement 2-seater would have taken its place. Would it have been the Fiero? The world will never know because the v8 is still very much alive and well, and getting stronger and more fuel effecient.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||02-23-2001||09:28 PM||||Pontiac hoped it would be. GM and Chevy wouldn't let it happen. That's why the Vette is still around and the Fiero isn't.<P>There was money issues also (not enough to go around), but Chevy is the crybaby and gets whatever it wants. And it doesn't care who gets screwed over.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||02-23-2001||09:43 PM||||There were plenty of rumors about the Fiero cutting into Corvette sales. But look at the real facts. The mid 80's Corvette was (is) the slowest years for the vette. In fact Chevy had to scramble in 87 to get the Corvette more HP because the competition between the F-bodies and Mustangs surpassed the Corvette's performance! The F-bodies with the 350's and Mustang's HP increase put the vehicles close to vette performance.<BR>I don't think that the Fiero drew sales away from the vette, but people who wanted a vette and could not afford it, bought the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ToddAsh||02-23-2001||10:15 PM||||I've got to add my Corvette/Fiero input.Over the years I've been lucky to own many Vettes from '56(still have) to a '91.People are impressed with Vettes and everyone tells you what a nice car you have,but I'm passed the point where I care what anyone else thinks.I drive what makes me smile.Last November I found a '85 V6 SE with 14,000 miles.This is without a doubt the most fun car to drive on a daily basis.Fiero owners can be PROUD.Mid-engine,4 wheel disks,2 passenger,space frame,composite body and more.I added new struts and shocks,16"wheels and tires,and I'll be putting on a rear sway bar as soon as my garage is warmer. If I wanted to drive a Vette it's sitting right there.I'll take the Fiero every time. Don't get me wrong,I know they can be dogs but the potential is right there.Just drove a '84 4 cyl and it was pretty bad but with a little work someone could have a really fun car.Anyway I'm grateful to have this Forum to be able to share our thoughts about this truly great little car. Todd Ash||||reg||1
Z||000007||v8vinnie||02-24-2001||09:43 PM||||yea, i can agree with you 100%, i too have owned a 81 c3, 97 c5, and am selling my 67 c2 corvette. i was a corvette finatic since 1983, but now i am a fiero finatic, my 87 gt ,t-tops and 5 speed, and that 345hp zz3 crate motor in the back, feels just like my 97 c5, not better but close, meaning i really dont feel inferior to any other sports car on the road, and makes me feel 30,000 dollars better!!!, i will always like corvettes but i really am having alot more fun for the money.||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||02-24-2001||11:02 PM||||As a Pontiac guy said to me (and supported by other GM people)........ GM is in the business to sell cars. Any cars. Money. The Fiero and Vette's are two different cars. A fast Fiero will pick up the lower budget market the Vette lost. The Fiero was killed due to sales. Vette was never worried about the Fiero. Different markets and pocket books. Few people would switch away from a Vette for any Fiero. If you can afford and want a Vette, the Fiero won't likely make you switch and it's unlikely you will upgrade from a Fiero to Vette if a Fiero is all you can afford.<BR>||||reg||1
